course: dictionary
lesson: 4887
title: Short words and word parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some short words are abbreviations, which are shortened forms of longer words. IG is one of these, and it can stand for different things. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «Are you on IG?» is about apps, because you can be on an app. In «won an Ig Nobel Prize in 2019», the word Prize tells you that Ig is part of an award name.
explain: Some letters are also part of longer words, like «pig» or «igloo». Check the spelling and the rest of the sentence before you decide what a short word means.
fact: An abbreviation is a shortened form of a word or name.
fact: IG is short for Instagram, a social media app for photos and videos.
fact: In texting, «ig» can be short for «I guess», which shows you are not sure.
fact: The Ig Nobel Prize is a joke prize for funny real science, a prize that makes people laugh, then think.
fact: Social media like IG usually has an age limit of 13 and up, so keep accounts private and do not share personal details.
exercise: «Are you on IG?» What does IG most likely mean here? | Inspector General, a person who checks rules | *Instagram, a social media app for photos and videos | I guess | Immunoglobulin, an antibody
exercise: Your friend texts «Pizza later? ig» What does ig mean? | Igloo | *I guess | Instagram | Inspector General
exercise: «Banana skins are slippery because of a gel on the inside; scientists who measured it won the joke Ig Nobel Prize in 2014.» What is the Ig Nobel Prize? | *A joke prize for funny real science | A prize for the fastest runner | A prize for the best banana | A serious science medal
test: «Wombats make cube-shaped droppings... the scientists who found this won an Ig Nobel Prize in 2019.» According to the sentence, why are the cubes useful? | They are soft and smell nice | They help wombats swim | *They do not roll off rocks and logs, so they work as signposts | They roll very fast down hills
test: Which word has ig as a word part, not as an abbreviation? | *igloo | Inspector General | IG | I guess
exam: Social media like IG usually has what age limit, and what should you do to stay safe? | *13 and up, so keep your account private and do not share personal details | No limit at all, so share your home address | 5 and up, so post everything you do | 18 and up only, so you never need privacy
